The volume of a right circular cone can be calculated using the formula $\frac{1}{3}\pi r_1h(r_1+r_2)$, where $r_1$ and $r_2$ are the radii of the large and small bases, respectively, and $h$ is the height.

Here, $r_1 = 8$ cm, $r_2 = 4$ cm, and $h = 6$ cm. Substituting these values into the formula, we get:

\begin{align*}
V &= \frac{1}{3}\pi \cdot 8 \cdot 6 (8+4) \\
&= 256 \pi
\end{align*}

Since $V=n\pi$, we have $n=256$.

\boxed{n=256}

